# ------------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
#
# `.env` is the one everybody remembers. The rest are the ones that actually
# leak: a key file dropped in the repo while testing the ssh provider, a
# service-account JSON downloaded from a cloud console, a `.netrc` written by
# some tool.
#
# Note what is deliberately NOT here: `.npmrc` is tracked, because it carries
# shared settings (fund=false, audit=false) -- and ignoring it would not help
# anyway, since ignore rules have no effect on a file git already follows.
# `npm login` writes `_authToken` into exactly that file, so it is covered by
# `scripts/secret-scan.mjs`, which reads tracked files and full history.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
.netrc
_netrc
credentials.json
service-account*.json
gha-creds-*.json

# --------------------------------------------------------------- husk runtime
#
# Computers, workspaces, audit logs and the downloaded Chromium live under
# ~/.husk, not in the repo -- but a `.husk/` appears here the moment anyone
# runs the CLI with HUSK_HOME pointed at the checkout, and each computer's
# browser is 325 MB unpacked.
.husk/
.husk-browser/

# The GitHub repo was cloned into the working tree as `husk/`, which puts a
# second `.git` inside this one. Committing it would add a gitlink nobody can
# resolve. Anchored to the root, so a future `packages/*/husk` would be fine.
/husk/

# ----------------------------------------------------- machine-local tool state
#
# Editor and assistant configuration that belongs to one machine, not to the
# project. Re-created in one command, and none of it is this repo's content.
.agents/

# Includes `worktrees/`, which are full duplicate checkouts. Committing it
# would put a second copy of the source tree inside the first one.
.claude/

# The lock file that goes with .agents/.
skills-lock.json

# ------------------------------------------------------------- scratch & junk
#
# `npm pack` leaves a tarball in whichever package directory it ran in, and
# `scripts/preflight.mjs` runs it eleven times.
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
*.bak
*.husk-bak
*.orig
*.rej
*~
*.log

# Ad-hoc scripts written at the repo root while debugging. Every one of these
# existed here at some point and none of them belong in a clone.
/probe*.mjs
/verify*.mjs
/persist*.mjs
/decisive.mjs

# --------------------------------------------------------------- test output
playwright-report/
test-results/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov

